## Two things to know

`runtime/cli/tests/level-contract-resolver.vitest.ts` is a fifth affected test that the brief did not name, and it now fails, 4 of 7:

```
 FAIL  tests/level-contract-resolver.vitest.ts > resolveLevelContract > keeps review lazy add-ons opt-in
- Expected  + Received
  [
    "handover.md",
    "timeline.md",
    "decision-record.md",
-   "resource-map.md",
  ]
```

It pins `'resource-map.md'` in the real manifest's lazy lists at lines 24, 47, 63, 73. I did not edit it because edits outside the named files are banned here. Either someone adds the four pins to a follow-up or that file goes back to the dispatcher.

Two leftovers are dead rather than broken. `frontmatter-migration.ts:139` still names the deleted template, but `readTemplateLiterals` wraps the read in `try/catch` and returns `{}` on failure, so a fill falls back to the document-class tables. `template-phrase-cleanup.mjs:42` keeps a `resourceMap` suffix that can no longer be reached, since no document class maps to that kind now.

Also, this worktree was being written by something else while I worked. `SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `references/`, `assets/`, `templates/README.md`, `feature-catalog`, `manual-testing-playbook` and `runtime/lib/validation/orchestrator.ts` all have 10:27 to 10:33 mtimes, and the doc references to `resource-map.md.tmpl` I found at the start were gone by my final grep without my touching them. I claim only the ten files listed above.
